 r←GetLinkSourceFolders namespaces;res;ind;i;col
⍝ Returns, for every name in `namespaces`, the folder Link has linked it to, and an empty vector for
⍝ any name that is not linked.\\
⍝ That folder is where Link keeps its `.linkconfig`, so it is what `HandleLinkSourceFlags` must be
⍝ given. `ListOpenProjects` cannot provide it: its second column is the project's HOME, and the two
⍝ differ whenever the config defines a "source" sub-folder, which is the normal case.\\
⍝ The column is found by its header, because the header depends on the Link version: Link 3
⍝ (Dyalog 18.2) reports three columns and calls it "Directory", while Link 4 (19.0 and later) calls it
⍝ "Source" and inserted a column for the direction arrow. A fixed index would name different things
⍝ on different interpreters, and under Link 3 it would hand over the number of objects.\\
⍝ Must be called while the projects are still linked: once the Link is broken Link has forgotten.
 r←(≢namespaces)⍴⊂''
 res←⎕SE.Link.Status''
 :If 2=⍴⍴res
     col←(res[1;]⍳'Source' 'Directory')~1+2⊃⍴res    ⍝ Whichever of the two this version of Link uses
     :If 0<≢col
         res←1↓res                                  ⍝ Drop the header row
         :If 0<≢res
             ind←(⎕C res[;1])⍳⎕C¨namespaces
             :For i :In ⍳≢namespaces
                 :If (i⊃ind)≤≢res
                     (i⊃r)←⊃res[i⊃ind;⊃col]
                 :EndIf
             :EndFor
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
